WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.744
SOC 2 is not solely the responsibility of security or compliance teams.

00:00:04.744 --> 00:00:08.227
A SOC 2 report reflects how the organization operates,

00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:12.485
which means many employees contribute to control performance and evidence quality.

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:17.129
Employees support SOC 2 by following policies, protecting information, using approved systems,

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:19.451
completing training, documenting work, reporting concerns,

00:00:19.451 --> 00:00:21.386
and respecting access control processes.

00:00:21.386 --> 00:00:25.643
Engineers and developers may contribute through secure development practices, code review,

00:00:25.643 --> 00:00:27.965
change management, logging, monitoring, vulnerability remediation,

00:00:27.965 --> 00:00:29.513
and incident response participation.

00:00:29.513 --> 00:00:32.609
Managers may contribute by approving access, reviewing responsibilities,

00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:34.932
ensuring training completion, supporting remediation work,

00:00:34.932 --> 00:00:37.254
and reinforcing expectations within their teams.

00:00:37.254 --> 00:00:39.576
HR, finance, legal, IT, security, operations,

00:00:39.576 --> 00:00:44.607
and customer-facing teams may all own or support controls depending on the scope.

00:00:44.607 --> 00:00:49.638
The exact responsibilities vary by organization, but the shared theme is consistent operation.

00:00:49.638 --> 00:00:50.799
Small behaviors matter.

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:56.218
Using a ticket instead of an informal message, recording an approval, closing a review,

00:00:56.218 --> 00:00:57.379
escalating an issue,

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:01.636
or completing training on time can all support evidence and accountability.

00:01:01.636 --> 00:01:06.280
A strong SOC 2 culture makes control performance part of normal work.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.924
People understand why the process exists, what record needs to be kept,

00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:14.794
and who to contact when something does not look right.

00:01:14.794 --> 00:01:19.439
This does not mean every employee needs to become a compliance specialist.

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:24.083
It means each person should understand the controls connected to their role

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:28.340
and treat process documentation as part of doing the job well.
